  "result": "Perfect! All 108 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js**:\n   - Added `lineVat(line)` to calculate VAT on the line amount after discount\n   - VAT is rounded per line using `roundCents()` and clamped at 0\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where `total = subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n\n2. **src/render.js**:\n   - Updated to show separate Subtotal, Discount, and VAT lines when applicable\n   - VAT line appears just above Total as specified\n   - Shows nothing when VAT is 0 (like VAT-exempt items)\n\n3. **Tests**: Added 18 new tests covering:\n   - VAT calculation on lines with/without discounts\n   - VAT rounding per line\n   - Different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n   - Mixed discounts and VAT\n   - Proper rendering of VAT in invoices\n\nThe key design decision: VAT is computed per line on the amount *after* the line's discount, then summed\u2014never calculated as a percentage of the invoice total.",
